{comment: Verse 1}
[Am]Are you going to [G]Scarborough [Am]Fair?
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[G]mary and [D]thyme;
Re[Am]member me to [C]one who lives [G]there,
She [Am]once was a [G]true love of [Am]mine.

{comment: Verse 2}
[Am]Tell her to make me a [G]cambric [Am]shirt,
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[G]mary and [D]thyme;
With[Am]out any [C]seam or needle[G]work,
Then [Em]she'll be a [G]true love of [Am]mine.
